SUMMARY:Improv 101 with Emily!
DESCRIPTION:Your Journey to the Stage Starts Here! About the Class: This is
  an 8 week long class that will teach the fundamentals of long form Improv
  Comedy. Topics covered include agreement with a scene partner\, character
  creation\, listening as a character and an actor\, and exploring the worl
 ds created in scenes. The class ends with a graduation show where the stud
 ents can show their friends and family the skills learned. Students must b
 e 18 or older for this class! This Class will run Mondays from 7pm-9pm on 
 the following dates: 10/19\, 10/26\, 11/2\, 11/9\, 11/16\, 11/23\, 11/30\,
  and 12/7 . This class has a class show on Saturday 12/12 at 3pm! Importan
 t: Please check your email the week prior to the start date of your class 
 for any updates. To qualify for the class show you must: Adhere to the Lan
 caster Improv Players' Code of Conduct. Attend at least six of the eight s
 essions (ideally all eight). Attend at least two improv shows during the l
 ength of the class. During the class you receive standby tickets for all o
 f our regular shows. These tickets get you into shows for free so long as 
 the show has not soldout! Tickets are on sale until 11:59pm of Friday 10/1
 6!\n\nPrice: Not supplied by this calendar\; check event details\n\nSchedu
